{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "class NewmanConwaySequence:\n    \"\"\"\n    Manages the recursive calculation and memoization of Newman-Conway sequence numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._cache = {1: 1, 2: 1}\n\n    def calculate(self, n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculates the nth Newman-Conway number using memoization.\n        \"\"\"\n        if n in self._cache:\n            return self._cache[n]\n\n        # P(n) = P(P(n-1)) + P(n-P(n-1))\n        p_n_minus_1 = self.calculate(n - 1)\n        \n        # Ensure that the arguments to recursive calls are valid indices\n        # The Newman-Conway sequence is defined for n >= 1.\n        # P(P(n-1)) and P(n-P(n-1)) must also refer to valid indices.\n        # This design assumes P(n-1) and n-P(n-1) will always be >= 1 for n > 2.\n        # For n=3: P(P(2)) + P(3-P(2)) = P(1) + P(3-1) = P(1) + P(2)\n        # All indices (1, 2) are >= 1.\n\n        p_n = self.calculate(p_n_minus_1) + self.calculate(n - p_n_minus_1)\n\n        self._cache[n] = p_n\n        return p_n\n_newman_conway_calculator = NewmanConwaySequence()\ndef sequence(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth number of the Newman-Conway sequence using a memoized helper.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a positive integer (n >= 1).\")\n    \n    return _newman_conway_calculator.calculate(n)"}
