{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "def odd_Equivalent(binary_string: str, rotations: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the number of times a binary string, when rotated a specified number of times,\n    results in a decimal equivalent that is an odd number.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _rotate_string(s: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Performs a single left rotation on a given string.\"\"\"\n        if not s:\n            return s\n        return s[1:] + s[0]\n\n    def _binary_to_decimal(binary_str: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Converts a binary string representation to its decimal integer equivalent.\"\"\"\n        return int(binary_str, 2)\n\n    def _is_odd(number: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Determines if an integer is an odd number.\"\"\"\n        return number % 2 != 0\n\n    odd_count = 0\n    current_string = binary_string\n\n    for _ in range(rotations):\n        decimal_value = _binary_to_decimal(current_string)\n        if _is_odd(decimal_value):\n            odd_count += 1\n        current_string = _rotate_string(current_string)\n\n    return odd_count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/113", "solution": "def check_integer(input_string: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the input string represents an integer.\n    An integer string consists solely of digits, optionally preceded by a single '+' or '-' sign.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_string:\n        return False\n\n    start_index = 0\n    if input_string[0] in ('+', '-'):\n        start_index = 1\n        if len(input_string) == 1:\n            return False\n\n    return input_string[start_index:].isdigit()"}
