{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "def lps(input_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the length of the longest palindromic subsequence in the given string.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(input_string, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n\n    n = len(input_string)\n\n    # dp[i][j] stores the length of the longest palindromic subsequence\n    # of the substring input_string[i...j]\n    dp = [[0 for _ in range(n)] for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # Every single character is a palindrome of length 1\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n\n    # Build the table.\n    # cl is current length of subsequence\n    for cl in range(2, n + 1):\n        for i in range(n - cl + 1):\n            j = i + cl - 1\n            if input_string[i] == input_string[j] and cl == 2:\n                dp[i][j] = 2\n            elif input_string[i] == input_string[j]:\n                dp[i][j] = 2 + dp[i + 1][j - 1]\n            else:\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i][j - 1], dp[i + 1][j])\n\n    return dp[0][n - 1]"}
