{"task_id": "Mbpp/264", "solution": "def dog_age(human_age: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates a dog's age in dog years based on human years.\n    The first two human years count as 10.5 dog years each, and subsequent years count as 4 dog years each.\"\"\"\n    if human_age <= 2:\n        # Each of the first two human years counts as 10.5 dog years\n        dog_years = human_age * 10.5\n    else:\n        # The first two human years are 2 * 10.5 = 21 dog years.\n        # Each subsequent human year after the second counts as 4 dog years.\n        dog_years = (2 * 10.5) + ((human_age - 2) * 4)\n    \n    return int(dog_years)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/261", "solution": "def division_elements(tuple1: tuple, tuple2: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"Performs element-wise division of two tuples, returning integer results for exact divisions.\n    For example: division_elements((10, 4, 6, 9),(5, 2, 3, 3)) == (2, 2, 2, 3).\n    \"\"\"\n    results = []\n    for i in range(len(tuple1)):\n        val1 = tuple1[i]\n        val2 = tuple2[i]\n\n        result = val1 / val2\n        if isinstance(val1, int) and isinstance(val2, int) and (val1 % val2 == 0):\n            results.append(int(result))\n        else:\n            results.append(result)\n    return tuple(results)"}
