{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "_memo = {}\ndef get_max_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the maximum sum for a given integer n using dynamic programming (memoization).\n    The function calculates f(n) = max((f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)), n).\n    \"\"\"\n    if n in _memo:\n        return _memo[n]\n\n    # Base case for recursion, when n is small, it will eventually hit 0, where f(0) = max(0,0)=0.\n    # For n=1, f(1) = max(f(0)+f(0)+f(0)+f(0), 1) = max(0, 1) = 1.\n    # The sum will inherently become 0 if all sub-problems are 0.\n    # This structure naturally handles n=0, 1, 2, ...\n    \n    # Calculate the sum of recursive calls\n    current_sum = get_max_sum(n // 2) + \\\n                  get_max_sum(n // 3) + \\\n                  get_max_sum(n // 4) + \\\n                  get_max_sum(n // 5)\n\n    # Determine the maximum between the current_sum and n itself\n    result = max(current_sum, n)\n\n    # Store the result in memoization cache before returning\n    _memo[n] = result\n    return result"}
