{"task_id": "Mbpp/415", "solution": "def max_Product(arr: list[int]) -> tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds a pair of integers with the highest product from a given array.\n    Handles arrays with fewer than two elements by returning an empty tuple.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(arr) < 2:\n        return ()\n\n    arr.sort()\n\n    # Calculate the product of the two smallest numbers (can be two large negative numbers)\n    product_of_smallest_two = arr[0] * arr[1]\n    pair_of_smallest_two = (arr[0], arr[1])\n\n    # Calculate the product of the two largest numbers\n    product_of_largest_two = arr[-1] * arr[-2]\n    pair_of_largest_two = (arr[-2], arr[-1]) # Ensure order (smaller, larger) for consistency\n\n    if product_of_smallest_two > product_of_largest_two:\n        return pair_of_smallest_two\n    else:\n        return pair_of_largest_two"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/420", "solution": "def cube_Sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of the cubes of the first 'n' even natural numbers.\n    Raises ValueError if 'n' is not a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be a positive integer\")\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        even_number = 2 * i\n        total_sum += even_number ** 3\n    return total_sum"}
