{"task_id": "Mbpp/445", "solution": "def index_multiplication(\n    tuple1: tuple[tuple[int, ...], ...],\n    tuple2: tuple[tuple[int, ...], ...]\n) -> tuple[tuple[int, ...], ...]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs index-wise multiplication of elements in two input tuples,\n    each containing nested tuples of integers.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input tuples must have the same number of nested tuples.\")\n\n    result_outer_tuple = []\n    for i in range(len(tuple1)):\n        sub_tuple1 = tuple1[i]\n        sub_tuple2 = tuple2[i]\n\n        if len(sub_tuple1) != len(sub_tuple2):\n            raise ValueError(f\"Nested tuples at index {i} must have the same number of elements.\")\n\n        result_inner_tuple = []\n        for j in range(len(sub_tuple1)):\n            result_inner_tuple.append(sub_tuple1[j] * sub_tuple2[j])\n        result_outer_tuple.append(tuple(result_inner_tuple))\n\n    return tuple(result_outer_tuple)"}
