{"task_id": "Mbpp/448", "solution": "def _get_nth_perrin_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Perrin number.\n    The Perrin sequence is defined by P(0)=3, P(1)=0, P(2)=2.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 3\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 2:\n        return 2\n    elif n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Perrin numbers are defined for non-negative integers.\")\n\n    memo = {0: 3, 1: 0, 2: 2}\n    for i in range(3, n + 1):\n        memo[i] = memo[i-2] + memo[i-3]\n    return memo[n]\ndef cal_sum(index: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of Perrin numbers from P(0) up to P(index), inclusive.\n    \"\"\"\n    if index < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Index must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    for i in range(index + 1):\n        total_sum += _get_nth_perrin_number(i)\n    return total_sum"}
