{"task_id": "Mbpp/454", "solution": "import re\ndef _clean_word(word: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Removes leading and trailing non-alphanumeric characters from a word.\n    This helper function ensures that punctuation around a word does not interfere with character matching.\n    \"\"\"\n    return re.sub(r'^\\W+|\\W+$', '', word)\ndef text_match_wordz(input_string: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the input string contains any word with the character 'z'.\n    Words are tokenized by whitespace, and leading/trailing punctuation is removed before checking.\n    \"\"\"\n    for raw_word in input_string.split():\n        cleaned_word = _clean_word(raw_word)\n        if 'z' in cleaned_word.lower():\n            return True\n    return False"}
