{"task_id": "Mbpp/457", "solution": "from typing import Any\ndef Find_Min(list_of_lists: list[list[Any]]) -> list[Any] | None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the sublist with the minimum length from a given list of lists.\n    Returns None if the input list of lists is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not list_of_lists:\n        return None\n\n    min_length = float('inf')\n    min_sublist = None\n\n    for sublist in list_of_lists:\n        current_sublist_length = len(sublist)\n        if current_sublist_length < min_length:\n            min_length = current_sublist_length\n            min_sublist = sublist\n            \n    return min_sublist"}
