{"task_id": "Mbpp/473", "solution": "def tuple_intersection(list1: list[tuple], list2: list[tuple]) -> set[tuple]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the order-agnostic intersection of two lists of tuples.\n    Tuples like (a, b) and (b, a) are considered identical for intersection purposes.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Helper function to convert a tuple into its canonical (sorted) form.\n    # This ensures order-agnostic comparison for tuples.\n    def _get_canonical_tuple(t: tuple) -> tuple:\n        return tuple(sorted(t))\n\n    canonical_set1 = set()\n    for t in list1:\n        canonical_set1.add(_get_canonical_tuple(t))\n\n    canonical_set2 = set()\n    for t in list2:\n        canonical_set2.add(_get_canonical_tuple(t))\n\n    return canonical_set1.intersection(canonical_set2)"}
